Description: Reject out-of-order slice segments and reset WPP row progress per slice
 A crafted stream that repeats or rewinds slice_segment_address re-ran CTB
 rows whose progress was already finished, so WPP row tasks stopped waiting
 for each other and double-freed the shared CABAC context. Such slice
 segments are now dropped, and each WPP slice segment resets the progress of
 the rows it decodes.
 Upstream adds DE265_WARNING_SLICE_SEGMENT_ADDRESS_NOT_INCREASING (1037).
 This backport reports DE265_WARNING_SLICE_SEGMENT_ADDRESS_INVALID instead so
 the public header and enum values stay as in Debian. It also leaves out the
 atomic de265_image::integrity change, which is unrelated to the fix.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/strukturag/libde265/commit/7803c6ebe65eaf631a543947fc76f4ab93929192
Bug: https://github.com/strukturag/libde265/security/advisories/GHSA-xp3h-6f5r-8cxp
Applied-Upstream: 1.1.2
Last-Update: 2026-11-26

